(footprint "FC-05B40P21H20" (version 20221018) (generator pcbnew)
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "BXCONN FC-05B40P21H20 (LCSC C23398824), 40-position 0.5mm-pitch dual-contact (top-and-bottom entry, 'no polarity') Flip-Top ZIF FPC connector, SMT right-angle. Hand-authored for pilink-4b6 (required pre-fab swap from the bottom-contact-only AFC01-S40FCA-00/C262674, which cannot mate the display FPC under this project's back-face contact-side working assumption -- see .research/findings/2026-11-15-display-fpc-contact-side.md). Pad pitch (0.5mm) and full 40-position span (DIMA = (N-1)*0.5mm = 19.5mm, pads at -9.75..+9.75mm) are read directly off this part's own CAD drawing (BXCONN dwg BX-CN-001-A, 'FC-05BNP21H20', title '0.5 Pitch H2.0 Backflip R/A Type CONN'), recovered in this environment by hand-decompressing the datasheet PDF's Flate-compressed content stream (no PDF rasterizer installed) and replaying its vector path/bezier operators with a small purpose-built interpreter -- not transcribed from a thumbnail. The drawing's own recommended-PCB-footprint detail additionally gives pad width 0.35mm+/-0.05 (X, used here in place of a guess) and confirms the 2.00mm 'Height Above Board' JLCPCB catalog field (section A-A). PIN-1 PHYSICAL LOCATION -- RESOLVED (pilink-4b6 fix round): independently confirmed via the EasyEDA/JLCPCB assembly-library footprint data for both parts (easyeda.com/api/products/<LCSC>/components, which answers a plain curl GET with no WAF block, unlike the easyeda.com website itself) -- this part's (C23398824) own JLC footprint places pad 1 (and its silkscreen pin-1 dot) at its RIGHT end, while the old AFC01-S40FCA-00's (C262674) JLC footprint places pad 1 at its LEFT end, both in the same canonical orientation (signal-pad row at the front edge, mounting tabs/body behind). This also agrees with the BXCONN drawing's own NO.1 marker (right end in its view 1). So the two parts number pin 1 from OPPOSITE physical ends. This footprint's pads are renumbered accordingly: pad '1' is now at the RIGHT end (x=+9.75, matching the real part), pad '40' at the LEFT (x=-9.75); the silkscreen pin-1 dot moved to match. Since ZIF contacts are straight-through, each PHYSICAL pad position keeps the SAME net it had before (net-to-physical-location assignment is unchanged) -- only the pad NUMBERING changed, and the schematic symbol's pin numbers (pico_link_custom:CFAF240320A0_FPC40) were mirror-renumbered in lockstep (pin k -> 41-k) so each signal still lands on the same physical pad position. Verified via an exported-netlist diff before/after: J501's physical pin-to-net mapping is unchanged. CABLE-ENTRY-SIDE CAVEAT (still open): whether the two parts' FPC cables insert from the same side relative to the pad row could not be confirmed from the EasyEDA footprint data, LCSC product photos, or JLC parametric fields (both show the same 'Flip-Top'/'Right Angle' convention with no explicit entry-side field, and the old part's datasheet has no dimensioned drawing) -- flagged for a human with physical samples before fab, independent of the now-resolved pin-1 question. DIMENSIONS -- mounting-pad (MP1/MP2) size/offset and signal-pad length corrected against the same EasyEDA footprint data (cross-checked against the BXCONN drawing's PCB-layout view): mounting tabs are 1.5mm wide x 2.5mm tall, centered at X=+/-11.45mm, 3.10mm from the signal pad row (not the prior placeholder 2.0x1.6mm at 2.68mm); signal pads are 1.5mm long (not 1.3mm). Body/courtyard Y-profile is still a reused placeholder from the old AFC01-S40FCA-00 footprint (same connector class/similar overall size: this part's own DIMB formula (N+8)*0.5+0.02 = 24.02mm overall width is close to that footprint's 24.4mm) -- not independently measured for this part. Needs a human KiCad-GUI DRC/visual pass before fab, same caveat class as every other hand-authored footprint in this project.")
